1306
00:52:27,438 --> 00:52:28,937
I hide when I hear the beeping.

1307
00:52:28,938 --> 00:52:30,277
- It's an instinct. - Why do you do that?

1308
00:52:30,278 --> 00:52:32,008
I have no idea why.

1309
00:52:32,278 --> 00:52:34,107
- Everyone does that. - I do that with Anju as well.

1310
00:52:34,108 --> 00:52:35,348
- I want to have fun. - Right.

1311
00:52:36,478 --> 00:52:38,517
- Gosh. How is my house? - This place is so nice.

1312
00:52:38,518 --> 00:52:39,748
I love this the most.

1313
00:52:39,918 --> 00:52:42,147
- The multi-cable? - I can see how you live.

1314
00:52:42,148 --> 00:52:44,288
- This is great. - Don't you use this? The 3m cable.

1315
00:52:44,458 --> 00:52:46,527
I didn't know there was a cable that was 3m long.

1316
00:52:46,528 --> 00:52:47,528
- You can find them. - This is great.

1317
00:52:47,529 --> 00:52:50,027
This completely changes the quality of life.

1318
00:52:50,028 --> 00:52:51,797
- It changes the quality of life? - Completely.

1319
00:52:51,798 --> 00:52:54,427
This one is 3m, and the one in the bedroom is also 3m.

1320
00:52:54,428 --> 00:52:58,398
My voice sounds bad as I had a sore throat that day.

1321
00:52:58,638 --> 00:53:01,007
- Let's say I was watching TV. - Right.

1322
00:53:01,008 --> 00:53:02,477
- Watching TV like this. - Watching TV and using your phone.

1323
00:53:02,478 --> 00:53:05,477
While watching TV, I can turn and place my phone here.

1324
00:53:05,478 --> 00:53:07,507
- Right. - Like this.

1325
00:53:07,508 --> 00:53:10,247
- And I fall asleep like this. - Gosh.

1326
00:53:10,248 --> 00:53:11,818
- That's true happiness. - Right.

1327
00:53:12,018 --> 00:53:13,918
Hey, you seem to be using that.

1328
00:53:14,088 --> 00:53:16,117
- That? I use it once in a while. - Right.

1329
00:53:16,118 --> 00:53:17,258
Show me.

1330
00:53:17,618 --> 00:53:18,817
- Hold on. - Do you really use it?

1331
00:53:18,818 --> 00:53:20,257
Well, I do,

1332
00:53:20,258 --> 00:53:22,128
but this is what's funny about it.

1333
00:53:22,428 --> 00:53:25,428
- There are different versions. - Right.

1334
00:53:25,968 --> 00:53:28,027
- The warm-up. - Right.

1335
00:53:28,028 --> 00:53:29,797
Look at him. He didn't use the pedals.

1336
00:53:29,798 --> 00:53:30,998
He won't use them at all.

1337
00:53:31,898 --> 00:53:33,668
(Let's see.)

1338
00:53:33,808 --> 00:53:36,907
This is what I do. Since the pedal comes off,

1339
00:53:36,908 --> 00:53:38,988
- I avoid using it like this. - Try using the pedal.

1340
00:53:40,278 --> 00:53:41,348
Try using the pedal.

1341
00:53:41,508 --> 00:53:43,377
(He places his feet on the pedals as Hyun Moo tells him to.)

1342
00:53:43,378 --> 00:53:45,458
- He didn't know about it. - I didn't know about it.

1343
00:53:47,048 --> 00:53:48,118
What?

1344
00:53:49,258 --> 00:53:50,288
What happened?

1345
00:53:50,558 --> 00:53:52,288
Moomoo's After-Sales Service!

1346
00:53:52,988 --> 00:53:53,988
What?

1347
00:53:55,028 --> 00:53:56,627
(Smiling brightly)

1348
00:53:56,628 --> 00:53:58,597
- What? - I changed the pedal.

1349
00:53:58,598 --> 00:54:00,238
- Really? - It's different now, isn't it?

1350
00:54:00,628 --> 00:54:01,927
- What? - I changed it.

1351
00:54:01,928 --> 00:54:03,037
How did you do that?

1352
00:54:03,038 --> 00:54:05,537
What do you mean? I said I was going to fix it.

1353
00:54:05,538 --> 00:54:07,307
- Gosh. - After the bazaar,

1354
00:54:07,308 --> 00:54:08,808
I felt bad about it.

1355
00:54:10,678 --> 00:54:11,837
You felt great, didn't you?

1356
00:54:11,838 --> 00:54:13,707
- He looked delighted. - I felt great.

1357
00:54:13,708 --> 00:54:15,547
Instead of fixing it in front of him,

1358
00:54:15,548 --> 00:54:17,377
it feels better as a pleasant surprise.

1359
00:54:17,378 --> 00:54:19,187
- Gosh. He's mischievous. - He always...

1360
00:54:19,188 --> 00:54:20,488
- Right. - The mischievous one.

1361
00:54:20,848 --> 00:54:22,317
I went around so much to look for the part.

1362
00:54:22,318 --> 00:54:23,587
You found this?

1363
00:54:23,588 --> 00:54:25,118
- I did. - Hold on.

1364
00:54:25,258 --> 00:54:27,458
I didn't know it was supposed to feel that comfortable.

1365
00:54:27,628 --> 00:54:29,228
It felt much easier.

1366
00:54:29,398 --> 00:54:31,097
Use it freely now.

1367
00:54:31,098 --> 00:54:33,128
- Gosh! This is amazing. - It's perfect now.

1368
00:54:33,368 --> 00:54:35,397
- What about the previous one? - It's right here.

1369
00:54:35,398 --> 00:54:37,168
- It's that one? - I got rid of it.

1370
00:54:37,568 --> 00:54:38,937
This one is new.

1371
00:54:38,938 --> 00:54:40,007
(He hands him a new part as a spare as well.)

1372
00:54:40,008 --> 00:54:41,938
- As a spare part? - Right.

1373
00:54:42,338 --> 00:54:43,937
- Change it when you need to. - Nice.

1374
00:54:43,938 --> 00:54:45,578
- That was nice of him. - Right.

1375
00:54:45,848 --> 00:54:47,947
- The left one would've been used. - Right.

1376
00:54:47,948 --> 00:54:49,447
He would have to come again if the left pedal broke.

1377
00:54:49,448 --> 00:54:51,017
- I'll place the mat for you. - Even a mat?

1378
00:54:51,018 --> 00:54:53,287
Right. Just in case.

1379
00:54:53,288 --> 00:54:55,418
- Gosh, this is perfect. - Right.

1380
00:54:55,618 --> 00:54:56,857
The machine won't make any noise for the house downstairs,

1381
00:54:56,858 --> 00:54:58,018
but this is just to be safe.

1382
00:54:58,588 --> 00:55:01,188
The machine barely makes any noise.

1383
00:55:01,258 --> 00:55:02,758
It's quiet.

1384
00:55:03,098 --> 00:55:04,327
These will be put together.

1385
00:55:04,328 --> 00:55:06,127
(He adjusts the pieces together.)

1386
00:55:06,128 --> 00:55:07,704
I thought this would be nice to place underneath.

1387
00:55:07,728 --> 00:55:11,698
(He gets everything done until the end.)

1388
00:55:13,108 --> 00:55:16,378
(Both pedals are working fine now.)

1389
00:55:17,278 --> 00:55:19,608
(Moomoo's After-Sales Service was perfect.)

1390
00:55:20,848 --> 00:55:22,608
I should buy things at the bazaar next time.

1391
00:55:23,318 --> 00:55:24,978
- Mine? - Not yours.

1392
00:55:26,118 --> 00:55:27,387
Since the after-sales service is really nice.

1393
00:55:27,388 --> 00:55:29,868
Right. I make sure to provide the perfect after-sales service.

1394
00:55:30,288 --> 00:55:33,088
- You should check the bedroom. - The bedroom?

1395
00:55:34,128 --> 00:55:36,898
This is the hot water mat you gave me.

1396
00:55:37,598 --> 00:55:39,698
After the pedal incident,

1397
00:55:39,828 --> 00:55:41,697
he felt so bad about it...

1398
00:55:41,698 --> 00:55:43,337
and sent me a hot water mat.

1399
00:55:43,338 --> 00:55:44,538
- Really? - Yes.

1400
00:55:45,398 --> 00:55:47,907
- The hot water mat. - You've been using it.

1401
00:55:47,908 --> 00:55:50,207
- It's nice, isn't it? - It's great.

1402
00:55:50,208 --> 00:55:51,677
I bought it without getting any discounts.

1403
00:55:51,678 --> 00:55:53,798
(He gets on the bed while showing the hot water mat.)

1404
00:55:54,948 --> 00:55:57,547
- Gosh! - It's nice, isn't it?

1405
00:55:57,548 --> 00:55:58,548
This feels great!

1406
00:55:59,148 --> 00:56:00,318
Gosh, I feel much better!

1407
00:56:01,618 --> 00:56:03,917
- Gosh. - At first...

1408
00:56:03,918 --> 00:56:05,188
(Woo Il turns toward the wall.)

1409
00:56:06,988 --> 00:56:09,258
(He slowly raises his arm.)

1410
00:56:11,098 --> 00:56:13,468
- What are you doing? - What are you doing?

1411
00:56:13,768 --> 00:56:15,888
(They share the warmth through their bodies instead.)

1412
00:56:16,838 --> 00:56:18,938
(It's cold in the winter, isn't it?)

1413
00:56:20,108 --> 00:56:23,678
(The day he lay with Ju Seung in one bed)

1414
00:56:24,308 --> 00:56:26,408
(It's been a while to be in bed with someone.)

1415
00:56:27,078 --> 00:56:28,647
(You know what I'm talking about, don't you?)

1416
00:56:28,648 --> 00:56:30,288
Look at Ju Seung keeping his eyes closed.

1417
00:56:31,848 --> 00:56:34,618
(When he got closer...)

1418
00:56:35,388 --> 00:56:37,018
- He's loving it. - He's disgusted.

1419
00:56:38,458 --> 00:56:39,487
Gosh.

1420
00:56:39,488 --> 00:56:41,488
(It's you today.)

1421
00:56:41,728 --> 00:56:43,027
I got goosebumps.

1422
00:56:43,028 --> 00:56:45,728
(His arm slowly goes around that man.)

1423
00:56:48,998 --> 00:56:51,098
(Shocked)

1424
00:56:51,498 --> 00:56:52,908
Gosh, that felt disgusting.

1425
00:56:53,468 --> 00:56:55,978
Just like with Sung Hwan,

1426
00:56:56,038 --> 00:56:57,778
- you're a killer. - Right.

1427
00:56:58,538 --> 00:57:01,078
(The two men enjoyed playing with water last summer.)

1428
00:57:02,048 --> 00:57:03,917
(A trembling touch)

1429
00:57:03,918 --> 00:57:05,018
(Shaking)

1430
00:57:05,548 --> 00:57:07,848
(Killer Moo only goes after the Rainbow Club members.)

1431
00:57:07,948 --> 00:57:09,918
I suddenly felt the scent of a man. Gosh.

1432
00:57:10,258 --> 00:57:11,417
In case you didn't eat,

1433
00:57:11,418 --> 00:57:13,527
- I brought something for you. - What did you bring?

1434
00:57:13,528 --> 00:57:15,958
I got up at 7am to make this.

1435
00:57:16,828 --> 00:57:18,158
You made it yourself?

1436
00:57:18,528 --> 00:57:19,968
What's the hottest thing these days?

1437
00:57:21,268 --> 00:57:22,298
Malatang?

1438
00:57:23,538 --> 00:57:25,458
Don't talk about something from eight years ago.

1439
00:57:25,538 --> 00:57:26,538
Tanghulu?

1440
00:57:26,608 --> 00:57:28,138
That was from 15 years ago.

1441
00:57:28,638 --> 00:57:30,907
What is something that is hard to get these days?

1442
00:57:30,908 --> 00:57:34,008
Oh, the DCK!

1443
00:57:34,478 --> 00:57:36,618
- The DCC, not the DCK. - Right. The DCC.

1444
00:57:37,018 --> 00:57:38,617
(You made the Dubai chewy cookie?)

1445
00:57:38,618 --> 00:57:39,718
Gosh.

1446
00:57:40,618 --> 00:57:42,788
- I've tried the DCC three times. - Right.

1447
00:57:43,558 --> 00:57:44,957
You really brought the DCC?

1448
00:57:44,958 --> 00:57:46,427
I've tried it once.

1449
00:57:46,428 --> 00:57:47,527
It's brown.

1450
00:57:47,528 --> 00:57:49,598
(Try the one I made.)

1451
00:57:50,028 --> 00:57:51,427
(The MCC appears.)

1452
00:57:51,428 --> 00:57:52,798
The MCC.

1453
00:57:54,468 --> 00:57:56,138
- What is this? - What do you mean?

1454
00:57:56,498 --> 00:57:58,498
Isn't this a sirutteok that is rolled into a ball?

1455
00:57:59,138 --> 00:58:00,707
How can you call it a sirutteok?

1456
00:58:00,708 --> 00:58:02,567
It looks like a sirutteok rolled into a ball.

1457
00:58:02,568 --> 00:58:04,337
It's chewy just like a sirutteok.

1458
00:58:04,338 --> 00:58:05,437
- The MCC. - The MCC?

1459
00:58:05,438 --> 00:58:06,477
I drew that as well.

1460
00:58:06,478 --> 00:58:08,877
(The MCC gets handed to him.)

1461
00:58:08,878 --> 00:58:10,998
Give it a try first. Give it a try and see how it is.

1462
00:58:11,248 --> 00:58:13,548
(He takes a big bite.)

1463
00:58:14,588 --> 00:58:16,258
I think it'll be really good.

1464
00:58:17,458 --> 00:58:20,428
(Chewing)

1465
00:58:20,588 --> 00:58:21,628
How is it?

1466
00:58:23,898 --> 00:58:26,297
(Crunchy)

1467
00:58:26,298 --> 00:58:27,428
It looks good.

1468
00:58:28,068 --> 00:58:29,098
It tastes good.

1469
00:58:29,198 --> 00:58:31,167
- It's good, isn't it? - It tastes good.

1470
00:58:31,168 --> 00:58:32,168
Right.

1471
00:58:32,169 --> 00:58:33,938
But the things inside are too big.

1472
00:58:34,568 --> 00:58:36,437
They're supposed to feel like powder inside.

1473
00:58:36,438 --> 00:58:37,737
(Embarrassed)

1474
00:58:37,738 --> 00:58:39,107
But they feel a bit too big.

1475
00:58:39,108 --> 00:58:40,108
It tastes good, though.

1476
00:58:40,109 --> 00:58:42,007
It's impossible to get...

1477
00:58:42,008 --> 00:58:43,277
- the noodle-like thing these days. - Right.

1478
00:58:43,278 --> 00:58:44,878
I made the noodles myself.

1479
00:58:45,378 --> 00:58:47,318
They became too thick like kalguksu noodles.

1480
00:58:47,988 --> 00:58:50,287
- That's why they feel that way. - I see. They feel this way...

1481
00:58:50,288 --> 00:58:52,094
- because they're too thick. - They feel too hard.

1482
00:58:52,118 --> 00:58:54,857
The kadayif was the fly in the ointment.

1483
00:58:54,858 --> 00:58:56,338
- That was the crucial part. - Right.

1484
00:58:56,398 --> 00:58:58,497
If I had bought the kadayif,

1485
00:58:58,498 --> 00:59:00,127
- it would've had that texture. - it would've felt the same.

1486
00:59:00,128 --> 00:59:02,867
- It's really hard to make. - It's really hard to make.

1487
00:59:02,868 --> 00:59:03,868
Right.

1488
00:59:05,238 --> 00:59:06,267
It's good, isn't it?

1489
00:59:06,268 --> 00:59:07,337
(The MCC has a different texture as it's handmade.)

1490
00:59:07,338 --> 00:59:09,607
- It's good. - It has so much pistachios in it.

1491
00:59:09,608 --> 00:59:10,708
It's good for you.

1492
00:59:12,178 --> 00:59:13,738
It's good when heated in the microwave.

1493
00:59:14,048 --> 00:59:15,247
I saw this somewhere.

1494
00:59:15,248 --> 00:59:16,377
- Really? - I heard it was good...

1495
00:59:16,378 --> 00:59:19,518
when heated in the microwave for ten seconds.

1496
00:59:19,648 --> 00:59:20,687
I didn't know that.

1497
00:59:20,688 --> 00:59:24,687
The reason for that is to make it gooey.

1498
00:59:24,688 --> 00:59:25,887
As it was already made to be gooey,

1499
00:59:25,888 --> 00:59:27,187
- it would've been good as is. - Right.

1500
00:59:27,188 --> 00:59:28,327
It was already gooey.

1501
00:59:28,328 --> 00:59:29,697
- It was already made that way? - Right.

1502
00:59:29,698 --> 00:59:31,127
- It makes it gooier. - So the thick ones...

1503
00:59:31,128 --> 00:59:32,627
- are heated up. - Right.

1504
00:59:32,628 --> 00:59:33,908
- It makes it smoother. - I see.

1505
00:59:34,668 --> 00:59:37,068
(The MCC was heated up.)

1506
00:59:38,068 --> 00:59:39,588
You heated it up with the plastic bag?

1507
00:59:39,908 --> 00:59:41,568
Yes. What's wrong with that?

1508
00:59:41,768 --> 00:59:43,208
It will stick to the plastic bag.

1509
00:59:43,638 --> 00:59:45,277
I don't think that's the problem.

1510
00:59:45,278 --> 00:59:46,308
Right.

1511
00:59:46,848 --> 00:59:48,508
- Gosh! - Gosh!

1512
00:59:49,448 --> 00:59:51,247
(Shocked)

1513
00:59:51,248 --> 00:59:52,318
Why is it like this?

1514
00:59:53,918 --> 00:59:55,917
- Gosh. - I heated it up for ten seconds.

1515
00:59:55,918 --> 00:59:57,318
You turned it into a big mess.

1516
00:59:57,618 --> 00:59:58,957
Why turn it into a big mess...

1517
00:59:58,958 --> 01:00:00,604
when I went through all that to make it for you?

1518
01:00:00,628 --> 01:00:02,668
I'm not lying. I just heated it up for ten seconds.

1519
01:00:02,798 --> 01:00:04,557
It was because you heated it up with the plastic bag.

1520
01:00:04,558 --> 01:00:06,167
(A disastrous sight)

1521
01:00:06,168 --> 01:00:08,628
Just pick it up and eat from the bag.

1522
01:00:09,268 --> 01:00:10,337
There you go.

1523
01:00:10,338 --> 01:00:11,398
(Stretching out)

1524
01:00:11,968 --> 01:00:13,537
(Disgusted)

1525
01:00:13,538 --> 01:00:14,708
Look at Hyun Moo's face!

1526
01:00:15,008 --> 01:00:16,008
There you go.

1527
01:00:16,009 --> 01:00:18,108
The marshmallow stretches out a lot more now.

1528
01:00:18,438 --> 01:00:20,448
- It tastes good, though. - Right. It tastes good.

1529
01:00:20,578 --> 01:00:23,348
I'm enjoying what you made like that.

1530
01:00:23,748 --> 01:00:25,177
Why would you look at me like that?

1531
01:00:25,178 --> 01:00:27,124
Heating it up for ten seconds doesn't seem like a good idea.

1532
01:00:27,148 --> 01:00:28,447
- It's just right. - It's just right, isn't it?

1533
01:00:28,448 --> 01:00:29,487
- Yes. - If it's too sweet...

1534
01:00:29,488 --> 01:00:31,318
The one I tried...

1535
01:00:31,618 --> 01:00:33,187
- was way too sweet. - Right.

1536
01:00:33,188 --> 01:00:35,487
I wondered why people enjoyed eating something so sweet.

1537
01:00:35,488 --> 01:00:36,804
That was the first impression I got from it.

1538
01:00:36,828 --> 01:00:38,188
- But this is just right. - Right.

1539
01:00:38,458 --> 01:00:41,328
(He takes another bite as it suits his taste.)

1540
01:00:42,198 --> 01:00:43,198
Gosh.

1541
01:00:44,238 --> 01:00:46,867
Why do you look so appalled?

1542
01:00:46,868 --> 01:00:48,638
Why are you looking at me like that?

1543
01:00:49,538 --> 01:00:52,178
He was tearing at it from the plastic bag.

1544
01:00:52,638 --> 01:00:54,977
But you didn't have to look at me like that.

1545
01:00:54,978 --> 01:00:56,047
I didn't realize my face was like that.

1546
01:00:56,048 --> 01:00:57,118
I was just eating it.

1547
01:00:57,948 --> 01:00:59,347
(Woo Il is really enjoying it.)

1548
01:00:59,348 --> 01:01:00,388
Right.

1549
01:01:01,318 --> 01:01:04,258
I've just been to Thailand recently.

1550
01:01:04,558 --> 01:01:07,187
You got me the hot water mat before I left.

1551
01:01:07,188 --> 01:01:09,158
- So out of gratitude... - What did you get me?

1552
01:01:10,158 --> 01:01:11,358
I got something hot.

1553
01:01:12,058 --> 01:01:13,428
I got something hot.

1554
01:01:13,798 --> 01:01:15,097
- You're not a big spender. - I'm curious.

1555
01:01:15,098 --> 01:01:16,567
- Right. Well, - Why bother?

1556
01:01:16,568 --> 01:01:18,567
- it's not the price that matters. - Right.

1557
