1806
01:10:05,572 --> 01:10:08,011
- As for Thai ramyeon... - You cried over a shopping bag.

1807
01:10:08,012 --> 01:10:10,441
As for the ramyeon, I was like, "Oh, you have this too."

1808
01:10:10,442 --> 01:10:11,712
But he bought the bag for me.

1809
01:10:12,112 --> 01:10:13,912
I also bought the ramyeon for you too.

1810
01:10:14,282 --> 01:10:15,751
(I know.)

1811
01:10:15,752 --> 01:10:17,652
You're sensitive to trends.

1812
01:10:17,982 --> 01:10:20,222
- It's hard to get this. - You're TSM.

1813
01:10:20,492 --> 01:10:21,551
Try holding it.

1814
01:10:21,552 --> 01:10:24,262
It suits your current outfit.

1815
01:10:25,362 --> 01:10:27,461
- It's perfect. - It does suit him.

1816
01:10:27,462 --> 01:10:28,562
Pistachio?

1817
01:10:28,862 --> 01:10:30,832
- Gosh. - Try carrying it.

1818
01:10:31,902 --> 01:10:33,771
- Do I look like a New Yorker? - The size is perfect too.

1819
01:10:33,772 --> 01:10:35,702
It's perfect. I really wanted this.

1820
01:10:35,972 --> 01:10:38,253
You should put MCC in it and sell them at people's homes.

1821
01:10:39,042 --> 01:10:40,071
I'm glad.

1822
01:10:40,072 --> 01:10:41,072
Actually, it doesn't cost much.

1823
01:10:41,073 --> 01:10:42,781
- It's really cheap. - It's not a matter of price.

1824
01:10:42,782 --> 01:10:44,241
- It's hard to get it. - You're right.

1825
01:10:44,242 --> 01:10:48,112
I put a special gift for you in the bag.

1826
01:10:48,352 --> 01:10:49,682
- Really? - Yes.

1827
01:10:50,222 --> 01:10:51,582
Oh, my!

1828
01:10:52,022 --> 01:10:53,221
Oh, my!

1829
01:10:53,222 --> 01:10:54,528
- What is it? - Something's in it.

1830
01:10:54,552 --> 01:10:56,892
I went to the Grammy Awards.

1831
01:10:57,092 --> 01:10:58,598
- What kind of cap is it? - He's the best.

1832
01:10:58,622 --> 01:10:59,762
It's a limited edition.

1833
01:11:00,892 --> 01:11:02,062
That's so cool.

1834
01:11:02,902 --> 01:11:04,601
Gosh, he's thriving.

1835
01:11:04,602 --> 01:11:05,701
(I'm proud of you.)

1836
01:11:05,702 --> 01:11:06,972
I hate them so much.

1837
01:11:07,402 --> 01:11:08,831
- Why? - Why didn't you win the award?

1838
01:11:08,832 --> 01:11:10,901
Why not give the award to you? I saw it.

1839
01:11:10,902 --> 01:11:12,711
The Grammy Awards was a really nice event...

1840
01:11:12,712 --> 01:11:14,511
even if I didn't win an award.

1841
01:11:14,512 --> 01:11:15,512
- That's right. - Of course.

1842
01:11:15,513 --> 01:11:18,182
So many excellent singers...

1843
01:11:18,612 --> 01:11:20,251
put on amazing performances,

1844
01:11:20,252 --> 01:11:22,282
so I soon forgot that I didn't win an award.

1845
01:11:22,382 --> 01:11:24,682
I really enjoyed it excitedly.

1846
01:11:25,022 --> 01:11:26,221
I'd never be able to get this.

1847
01:11:26,222 --> 01:11:28,391
- A true musician. World-class. - That's really cool.

1848
01:11:28,392 --> 01:11:29,921
Of course it is. It's impossible to get it.

1849
01:11:29,922 --> 01:11:31,368
- It's impossible for Hyun Moo. - What is this?

1850
01:11:31,392 --> 01:11:33,732
It's a Grammy Awards T-shirt.

1851
01:11:34,262 --> 01:11:36,031
- How did you know I like these? - The emblem is cute.

1852
01:11:36,032 --> 01:11:38,101
I just thought you'd like things like this.

1853
01:11:38,102 --> 01:11:41,372
- He's staring intently. - You can only get these there.

1854
01:11:41,732 --> 01:11:42,842
Oh, my.

1855
01:11:44,272 --> 01:11:45,541
(Shocked)

1856
01:11:45,542 --> 01:11:47,842
- What is it? - I love it. How crazy. It's so hip.

1857
01:11:48,112 --> 01:11:49,581
- It's a pistachio look. - A badge.

1858
01:11:49,582 --> 01:11:50,682
- A badge? - A badge.

1859
01:11:52,342 --> 01:11:54,381
- You really can't get that. - You really can't.

1860
01:11:54,382 --> 01:11:56,222
(Sulky)

1861
01:11:56,422 --> 01:11:58,021
This is really special.

1862
01:11:58,022 --> 01:12:00,921
- On the day of the award, - How many gifts did he get?

1863
01:12:00,922 --> 01:12:03,462
They gave out chocolate in case we got hungry.

1864
01:12:03,992 --> 01:12:05,362
But I just brought it back.

1865
01:12:05,492 --> 01:12:06,631
I still haven't had it.

1866
01:12:06,632 --> 01:12:08,732
- It's better if you don't. - It's pretty.

1867
01:12:09,502 --> 01:12:11,162
It's so pretty. I'm about to die.

1868
01:12:11,832 --> 01:12:13,752
It's driving me crazy. I love things like these.

1869
01:12:14,172 --> 01:12:15,702
I'm about to get upset.

1870
01:12:16,642 --> 01:12:18,941
The ramyeon is expensive too. It's from another country.

1871
01:12:18,942 --> 01:12:21,542
Of course. I'm eating it well. I had three already.

1872
01:12:21,672 --> 01:12:23,232
I'm eating it while thinking about you.

1873
01:12:24,512 --> 01:12:26,312
I got such good gifts from you.

1874
01:12:26,482 --> 01:12:27,782
Not at all.

1875
01:12:27,882 --> 01:12:29,551
Gosh, I'll keep them well.

1876
01:12:29,552 --> 01:12:32,722
You gave me a nice keyboard, so you deserve them.

1877
01:12:32,992 --> 01:12:34,791
- Actually, I... - Yes?

1878
01:12:34,792 --> 01:12:35,922
What? Is someone here?

1879
01:12:36,262 --> 01:12:37,362
It must be my food.

1880
01:12:38,222 --> 01:12:39,532
You ordered something?

1881
01:12:39,762 --> 01:12:41,331
- He ordered food. - You're eating again?

1882
01:12:41,332 --> 01:12:42,831
- I haven't eaten yet, so... - You haven't?

1883
01:12:42,832 --> 01:12:44,401
It's late lunch, but...

1884
01:12:44,402 --> 01:12:45,702
I came at the right timing.

1885
01:12:46,032 --> 01:12:47,372
I ordered some sushi.

1886
01:12:48,402 --> 01:12:49,942
He ordered food that doesn't smell.

1887
01:12:50,272 --> 01:12:51,872
I wonder how his house smells.

1888
01:12:52,172 --> 01:12:55,012
- It's not too much. It's subtle. - The scent is all over?

1889
01:12:55,172 --> 01:12:57,541
Like an automatic diffuser. You know what it is, right?

1890
01:12:57,542 --> 01:12:59,612
- I know. - Like the ones in bathrooms.

1891
01:12:59,782 --> 01:13:01,262
- How... - What about Woo Il's place?

1892
01:13:01,512 --> 01:13:02,882
It smelled like my parents' place.

1893
01:13:03,052 --> 01:13:05,581
It was nice too. The warm smell of a parents' place.

1894
01:13:05,582 --> 01:13:06,892
Woo Il is upset.

1895
01:13:07,192 --> 01:13:09,291
Next time you come to my place, I'll put the diffuser...

1896
01:13:09,292 --> 01:13:11,092
on your philtrum as soon as you enter.

1897
01:13:11,722 --> 01:13:14,282
- I'll apply it myself before going. - It'll smell nice all day.

1898
01:13:14,392 --> 01:13:16,832
(I'll serve you properly next time.)

1899
01:13:17,162 --> 01:13:19,271
- I ordered a lot. - You did?

1900
01:13:19,272 --> 01:13:20,572
I think you can eat with me.

1901
01:13:20,832 --> 01:13:23,742
Sure. You should hurry up and eat.

1902
01:13:24,972 --> 01:13:28,072
Gosh, things like this too. It's beautifully placed.

1903
01:13:28,442 --> 01:13:30,911
Where did you get a plate like this?

1904
01:13:30,912 --> 01:13:32,652
It's a dish I really like.

1905
01:13:32,882 --> 01:13:34,912
Gosh, how do I develop tastes like this?

1906
01:13:35,552 --> 01:13:37,021
- Even the lamp is hip. - It's so nice.

1907
01:13:37,022 --> 01:13:38,342
- I know. - Your house is so hip.

1908
01:13:39,252 --> 01:13:41,721
(Impressed)

1909
01:13:41,722 --> 01:13:44,562
Hyun Moo, there are different kinds.

1910
01:13:44,862 --> 01:13:47,032
Eat whichever piece you want.

1911
01:13:47,192 --> 01:13:48,931
(He plated the sushi nicely too.)

1912
01:13:48,932 --> 01:13:51,102
- He plated them nicely. - He even plated them for me.

1913
01:13:52,672 --> 01:13:54,902
(Taking a sip of water first)

1914
01:13:55,272 --> 01:13:56,842
(Taking a glance)

1915
01:13:57,072 --> 01:13:58,172
Where's that cup from?

1916
01:13:58,572 --> 01:14:02,112
Actually, it's five dollars each.

1917
01:14:02,942 --> 01:14:04,741
- It looks expensive for no reason. - It's not expensive.

1918
01:14:04,742 --> 01:14:06,082
It was around 5 or 8 dollars.

1919
01:14:06,982 --> 01:14:08,112
It's not expensive.

1920
01:14:08,652 --> 01:14:09,772
This one's expensive, right?

1921
01:14:10,522 --> 01:14:13,392
This one? It was only a few tens of dollars.

1922
01:14:14,052 --> 01:14:16,492
I couldn't find a vase like this. I recently got one.

1923
01:14:16,662 --> 01:14:17,691
Right.

1924
01:14:17,692 --> 01:14:19,122
This one's a few dollars too.

1925
01:14:19,292 --> 01:14:21,532
- Where did you get it? - From Today House.

1926
01:14:22,032 --> 01:14:24,132
None of the things I use is expensive.

1927
01:14:24,962 --> 01:14:27,032
How come my things are expensive but not pretty?

1928
01:14:28,032 --> 01:14:29,202
What's wrong with my taste?

1929
01:14:29,542 --> 01:14:32,042
(Feeling bitter for no reason)

1930
01:14:33,642 --> 01:14:37,182
(Shall I try the sushi now?)

1931
01:14:39,382 --> 01:14:40,882
I was hungry.

1932
01:14:41,352 --> 01:14:43,182
(Exclaiming)

1933
01:14:43,652 --> 01:14:45,198
You got them from a nice sashimi place.

1934
01:14:45,222 --> 01:14:46,421
- Really? It's good to hear. - Yes.

1935
01:14:46,422 --> 01:14:48,062
- Even the sashimi was nice. - It's good.

1936
01:14:48,252 --> 01:14:49,862
- Come on! - Come on!

1937
01:14:50,622 --> 01:14:53,292
- Did you dip it in a diffuser? - You're too much.

1938
01:14:53,462 --> 01:14:55,132
Did you dip it in a diffuser or what?

1939
01:14:55,492 --> 01:14:56,862
It's not even by the seaside.

1940
01:14:57,262 --> 01:14:59,022
It doesn't feel like sashimi by the seaside.

1941
01:14:59,132 --> 01:15:00,292
It was more like fine dining.

1942
01:15:00,572 --> 01:15:02,492
He only got complimented for the charging cable.

1943
01:15:02,872 --> 01:15:04,041
"The 3m cable is nice."

1944
01:15:04,042 --> 01:15:06,572
(The only thing that caught Hyun Moo's eye, 3m cable)

1945
01:15:07,012 --> 01:15:10,012
What would you have done if it wasn't for the 3m charging cable?

1946
01:15:10,612 --> 01:15:12,382
(Goodness)

1947
01:15:12,482 --> 01:15:14,481
- I should've bought it for you. - Don't worry.

1948
01:15:14,482 --> 01:15:15,912
(He's having another piece.)

1949
01:15:16,882 --> 01:15:18,852
(Taking a glance)

1950
01:15:19,692 --> 01:15:21,552
(Hesitating)

1951
01:15:22,392 --> 01:15:25,162
- You didn't get to eat? - No.

1952
01:15:26,292 --> 01:15:28,762
(Staring)

1953
01:15:30,402 --> 01:15:34,471
(Hue dips it in soy sauce.)

1954
01:15:34,472 --> 01:15:35,602
You didn't have breakfast?

1955
01:15:36,242 --> 01:15:37,672
Just a bit.

1956
01:15:37,902 --> 01:15:40,341
I did some work that required some thinking.

1957
01:15:40,342 --> 01:15:42,118
(He eats it straight without dipping in the soy sauce.)

1958
01:15:42,142 --> 01:15:43,912
(Taking a peek)

1959
01:15:44,582 --> 01:15:46,912
- Why? Do you feel uncomfortable? - What's wrong?

1960
01:15:47,512 --> 01:15:48,611
I got nervous.

1961
01:15:48,612 --> 01:15:51,051
I paid so much attention when I ate at Hue's place...

1962
01:15:51,052 --> 01:15:53,228
- in case I dropped something. - Oh, in case you dropped something.

1963
01:15:53,252 --> 01:15:56,322
He poured soy sauce for me, but I didn't dip it once.

1964
01:15:56,892 --> 01:15:59,731
I didn't want to drop soy sauce on his white table,

1965
01:15:59,732 --> 01:16:01,532
so I didn't dip it and ate it bland.

1966
01:16:01,762 --> 01:16:03,162
That's how much attention I paid.

1967
01:16:03,532 --> 01:16:05,532
I felt uncomfortable, actually.

1968
01:16:06,032 --> 01:16:08,901
But for Woo Il's place, even if I spill the whole soy sauce,

1969
01:16:08,902 --> 01:16:10,582
I feel like I can just wipe it with a rag.

1970
01:16:11,002 --> 01:16:12,042
That's how his house is.

1971
01:16:13,012 --> 01:16:16,071
(Woo Il's place felt comfortable as though it was his.)

1972
01:16:16,072 --> 01:16:17,232
You fall asleep easily there.

1973
01:16:18,542 --> 01:16:21,352
Soon, there could be a new production...

1974
01:16:21,982 --> 01:16:24,751
- with the piece you write, then. - Well, but...

1975
01:16:24,752 --> 01:16:27,291
You don't really watch out for things like that, but you do there.

1976
01:16:27,292 --> 01:16:28,922
That's how neat his house was.

1977
01:16:31,062 --> 01:16:33,332
Remember how you came into my house with your shoes on?

1978
01:16:37,232 --> 01:16:39,578
Your place's interior design was like that of an American home.

1979
01:16:39,602 --> 01:16:41,302
What American home? It was an apartment!

1980
01:16:42,842 --> 01:16:44,041
There are certain charms...

1981
01:16:44,042 --> 01:16:45,201
- that comfortable homes give. - That's right.

1982
01:16:45,202 --> 01:16:46,412
My house is comfortable too.

1983
01:16:46,572 --> 01:16:48,972
I think I'd feel uncomfortable if Hue told me to live there.

1984
01:16:49,712 --> 01:16:51,842
- I can't do things freely. - That's right.

1985
01:16:52,342 --> 01:16:53,851
Then if you had a choice, you'd live at mine?

1986
01:16:53,852 --> 01:16:54,882
Of course.

1987
01:16:55,182 --> 01:16:56,222
I'll make a mess.

1988
01:16:59,422 --> 01:17:00,492
Today,

1989
01:17:01,822 --> 01:17:03,162
I made something...

1990
01:17:03,992 --> 01:17:05,321
to give to you.

1991
01:17:05,322 --> 01:17:07,062
What? What did you make?

1992
01:17:07,092 --> 01:17:09,662
What's the most popular food in Korea...

1993
01:17:09,862 --> 01:17:11,032
- these days? - DCQ.

1994
01:17:11,302 --> 01:17:12,832
- DCC. - Oh, he knows.

1995
01:17:13,802 --> 01:17:14,832
Correct.

1996
01:17:14,972 --> 01:17:16,672
You made it yourself?

1997
01:17:17,172 --> 01:17:18,301
I did.

1998
01:17:18,302 --> 01:17:19,612
- You made it yourself? - Yes.

1999
01:17:20,172 --> 01:17:21,671
I tried it for the first time the day before yesterday.

2000
01:17:21,672 --> 01:17:22,672
From where?

2001
01:17:22,982 --> 01:17:25,141
I went to Busan...

2002
01:17:25,142 --> 01:17:26,512
for a show there.

2003
01:17:26,882 --> 01:17:29,111
Actress Park Jin Joo ordered it for me.

2004
01:17:29,112 --> 01:17:30,182
- Jin Joo did? - Yes.

2005
01:17:30,922 --> 01:17:31,982
I can't wait to try it.

2006
01:17:33,792 --> 01:17:37,422
(About to open Moo chewy cookies)

2007
01:17:38,262 --> 01:17:39,391
Moo chewy cookies.

2008
01:17:39,392 --> 01:17:41,492
I have my own artistic world.

2009
01:17:42,062 --> 01:17:44,332
I can't help but reflect on myself. The creative...

2010
01:17:44,702 --> 01:17:46,902
The creative energy...

2011
01:17:47,572 --> 01:17:50,041
I wonder if I'm releasing enough of it. I'm reflecting on myself.

2012
01:17:50,042 --> 01:17:51,162
It sparks such urges, right?

2013
01:17:51,902 --> 01:17:53,102
"It sparks such urges, right?"

2014
01:17:54,342 --> 01:17:56,582
Also, I wrapped it in a hip style.

2015
01:17:58,412 --> 01:18:00,452
(Rustling)

2016
01:18:00,512 --> 01:18:02,952
The plastic bag is a bit... Wait, Hyun Moo.

2017
01:18:07,622 --> 01:18:08,692
Isn't it hip?

2018
01:18:09,292 --> 01:18:10,822
It really doesn't suit that house.

2019
01:18:11,962 --> 01:18:13,631
Hey, this is what you call hip.

2020
01:18:13,632 --> 01:18:16,091
Wrapping it roughly.

2021
01:18:16,092 --> 01:18:18,162
When you took it out...

2022
01:18:18,902 --> 01:18:21,901
When you walk your dog...

2023
01:18:21,902 --> 01:18:23,471
- Goodness. - Everyone thinks the same.

2024
01:18:23,472 --> 01:18:24,841
- And the color had to be this. - Right.

2025
01:18:24,842 --> 01:18:26,942
And the bag had to be that.

2026
01:18:27,572 --> 01:18:30,312
But... Even if it looks bad,

2027
01:18:31,112 --> 01:18:33,952
once you eat it... I made these since 7am.

2028
01:18:34,352 --> 01:18:36,252
Don't think it like that.

2029
01:18:36,722 --> 01:18:38,522
(Dropped)

2030
01:18:39,422 --> 01:18:40,692
It was heavy.

2031
01:18:43,562 --> 01:18:45,461
- No, that's a prejudice. - I mean...

2032
01:18:45,462 --> 01:18:46,791
Hurry up and get that bag away.

2033
01:18:46,792 --> 01:18:48,962
Okay. It's gone.

2034
01:18:49,602 --> 01:18:51,861
Its stickiness is...

2035
01:18:51,862 --> 01:18:53,748
(Moo chewy cookie's first impression is strong.)

2036
01:18:53,772 --> 01:18:55,131
- But... - Yes.

2037
01:18:55,132 --> 01:18:56,901
It tastes and smells completely different.

2038
01:18:56,902 --> 01:18:58,572
You'll be surprised once you smell it.

2039
01:18:58,802 --> 01:19:00,612
(Sniffing)

2040
01:19:00,912 --> 01:19:02,841
- The chocolate smell is rich. - I added cocoa.

2041
01:19:02,842 --> 01:19:04,342
I used high-quality pistachios.

2042
01:19:05,712 --> 01:19:08,012
- Gosh, it's really... - Gosh, the sound.

2043
01:19:08,212 --> 01:19:10,082
It's not even sand. It's like glass.

2044
01:19:11,082 --> 01:19:13,551
I added a thick layer of kadayif.

2045
01:19:13,552 --> 01:19:14,721
How come it's so thick?

2046
01:19:14,722 --> 01:19:16,662
- It's like pebbles. - I'll try it.

2047
01:19:17,992 --> 01:19:20,432
(Crunch)

2048
01:19:21,232 --> 01:19:23,602
(Nervous)

2049
01:19:24,702 --> 01:19:26,631
(Exclaiming)

2050
01:19:26,632 --> 01:19:27,832
It's good.

2051
01:19:28,602 --> 01:19:30,301
It's better than the one I had in Busan.

2052
01:19:30,302 --> 01:19:32,241
(Amazed)

2053
01:19:32,242 --> 01:19:34,802
- It's better than the real one. - It suits my taste way better.

2054
01:19:35,372 --> 01:19:36,542
It's really good.

2055
01:19:36,742 --> 01:19:37,982
Writer Hue.

2056
01:19:38,642 --> 01:19:40,751
If the fillings were hard...

2057
01:19:40,752 --> 01:19:42,451
- That hit his taste exactly. - That's right.

2058
01:19:42,452 --> 01:19:43,581
I know.

2059
01:19:43,582 --> 01:19:44,781
The New Yorker approved of it.

2060
01:19:44,782 --> 01:19:46,321
(He likes the thick kadayif better.)

2061
01:19:46,322 --> 01:19:47,391
- This... - It's really good.

2062
01:19:47,392 --> 01:19:49,421
It's really hard to make them thin.

2063
01:19:49,422 --> 01:19:50,892
I had to squeeze it really hard.

2064
01:19:51,322 --> 01:19:53,162
The wetness had to be just right.

2065
01:19:53,662 --> 01:19:55,761
The cloth needs to have small holes too.

2066
01:19:55,762 --> 01:19:57,862
And you have to be skilled too.

2067
01:19:58,132 --> 01:19:59,831
Can you give about three more?

2068
01:19:59,832 --> 01:20:01,101
- You see? - Gosh.

2069
01:20:01,102 --> 01:20:02,201
You know he really liked it that he asked for more.

2070
01:20:02,202 --> 01:20:03,271
That's praise.

2071
01:20:03,272 --> 01:20:04,601
If he wants more, that means he really likes it.

2072
01:20:04,602 --> 01:20:05,602
It's really good.

2073
01:20:05,603 --> 01:20:06,842
I feel so proud.

2074
01:20:07,442 --> 01:20:11,082
Hue is the type of person who's straightforward.

2075
01:20:11,212 --> 01:20:14,181
And he must be more cool-headed toward cookies...

2076
01:20:14,182 --> 01:20:16,481
since he lives in the US too.

2077
01:20:16,482 --> 01:20:17,522
That's a prejudice.

2078
01:20:17,582 --> 01:20:19,542
I'm so strongly deferential to foreign countries.

2079
01:20:19,692 --> 01:20:21,421
Besides saying it was good,

2080
01:20:21,422 --> 01:20:23,821
he asked if I had more.

2081
01:20:23,822 --> 01:20:25,122
That means...

2082
01:20:25,562 --> 01:20:27,392
the domestic market is too small for me.

2083
01:20:27,532 --> 01:20:28,962
If I have time,

2084
01:20:29,432 --> 01:20:31,762
I'll open a pop-up store...

2085
01:20:32,562 --> 01:20:33,922
in front of a theater in New York.

2086
01:20:34,502 --> 01:20:35,832
They'll love it so much.

2087
01:20:36,332 --> 01:20:38,652
- They'll wait in line for sure. - I can name it K-cookie.

2088
01:20:39,572 --> 01:20:41,172
Do you like matcha too?

2089
01:20:41,712 --> 01:20:42,772
Of course.

2090
01:20:43,282 --> 01:20:44,342
I love matcha.

2091
01:20:45,982 --> 01:20:47,282
Hyun Moo, this...

2092
01:20:48,912 --> 01:20:51,882
Isn't this the bottom?

2093
01:20:52,982 --> 01:20:54,692
I found that out for the first time.

2094
01:20:55,822 --> 01:20:57,191
I see!

2095
01:20:57,192 --> 01:20:58,921
I think the sticker should be here.

2096
01:20:58,922 --> 01:21:00,361
Oh, this is the top.

2097
01:21:00,362 --> 01:21:01,631
Yes, since this is the top...

2098
01:21:01,632 --> 01:21:03,132
It was my first time using it.

2099
01:21:03,732 --> 01:21:05,562
It's more hip that way.

2100
01:21:05,962 --> 01:21:07,201
This is the cover.

2101
01:21:07,202 --> 01:21:08,732
You're right.

2102
01:21:09,332 --> 01:21:11,801
- This is the top. - I thought something was off.

2103
01:21:11,802 --> 01:21:13,041
This is modern art too.

2104
01:21:13,042 --> 01:21:15,171
- Is that so? - Modern art?

2105
01:21:15,172 --> 01:21:16,612
- Right? - Because of the picture...

2106
01:21:16,812 --> 01:21:19,212
You can have that later.

2107
01:21:21,012 --> 01:21:22,582
(Ta-da!)

2108
01:21:25,622 --> 01:21:26,751
(Moomoo's after-service for Hue)

2109
01:21:26,752 --> 01:21:28,622
You bought a pedal from Yamaha?

2110
01:21:28,722 --> 01:21:30,338
- Because the keyboard is Yamaha's. - Why?

2111
01:21:30,362 --> 01:21:32,421
- Why? - Even musicians...

2112
01:21:32,422 --> 01:21:34,032
buy the cheapest pedal.

2113
01:21:34,432 --> 01:21:35,631
- I shouldn't have bought that. - Because...

2114
01:21:35,632 --> 01:21:37,162
(Joking)

2115
01:21:37,262 --> 01:21:38,731
- That'd make him happy. - Since you were getting it anyway.

2116
01:21:38,732 --> 01:21:39,831
- The authentic one. - Right.

2117
01:21:39,832 --> 01:21:43,202
I showed him the logo on the box on purpose.

2118
01:21:43,302 --> 01:21:44,942
To emphasize that it's authentic.

2119
01:21:45,872 --> 01:21:48,171
- You got the authentic one. - Of course.

2120
01:21:48,172 --> 01:21:49,471
- He recognized it. - He did.

2121
01:21:49,472 --> 01:21:51,753
- "You got the authentic one." - It was money well spent.

2122
01:21:51,912 --> 01:21:53,782
Let me try attaching it.

2123
01:21:56,412 --> 01:21:57,782
Hyun Moo, you're like Santa.

2124
01:21:57,982 --> 01:22:00,051
It made me really happy to go around giving out gifts.

2125
01:22:00,052 --> 01:22:01,252
- You will? - Yes.

2126
01:22:01,922 --> 01:22:03,791
- Shall I attach it? - Yes.

2127
01:22:03,792 --> 01:22:07,462
(Let's quickly attach it.)

2128
01:22:08,632 --> 01:22:11,401
I haven't been able to play it at all,

2129
01:22:11,402 --> 01:22:12,702
so I was quite sad.

2130
01:22:14,732 --> 01:22:16,072
It's as good as new.

2131
01:22:16,972 --> 01:22:19,472
- The after-service is amazing. - Gosh.

2132
01:22:19,702 --> 01:22:21,412
I love it.

2133
01:22:21,612 --> 01:22:22,912
Can you play any piece?

2134
01:22:23,182 --> 01:22:25,042
You need to make a masterpiece on that.

2135
01:22:25,712 --> 01:22:29,111
I only played the piano when I was young,

2136
01:22:29,112 --> 01:22:31,721
so I started taking a piano lesson again after 30 years.

2137
01:22:31,722 --> 01:22:33,592
He's learning to play the piano again.

2138
01:22:34,092 --> 01:22:36,661
- Whose piece will you play? - It's by Bach.

2139
01:22:36,662 --> 01:22:37,992
- Bach. - Bach.

2140
01:22:39,462 --> 01:22:40,831
Now, the piano is being used.

2141
01:22:40,832 --> 01:22:42,162
(Amazed)

2142
01:22:42,532 --> 01:22:43,862
It met its rightful owner.

2143
01:22:48,902 --> 01:22:51,402
(In a trance)

2144
01:22:53,242 --> 01:22:55,072
It's like "Whiplash."

2145
01:22:56,442 --> 01:22:58,522
(Dipping in his sentimentality instead of soy sauce)

2146
01:22:59,882 --> 01:23:02,512
(Yes, this is what I wanted.)

2147
01:23:04,122 --> 01:23:05,782
(This is it!)

2148
01:23:07,222 --> 01:23:09,092
(Dumbfounded)

2149
01:23:11,192 --> 01:23:14,062
(I can't believe my piano is being used like this!)

2150
01:23:15,862 --> 01:23:17,402
It met the right owner.

2151
01:23:17,502 --> 01:23:18,532
That's classy.

2152
01:23:18,862 --> 01:23:20,472
Yes, Hue.

2153
01:23:20,732 --> 01:23:22,272
What time is your flight tomorrow?

2154
01:23:22,372 --> 01:23:24,341
It's an evening flight.

2155
01:23:24,342 --> 01:23:25,771
So I need to start...

2156
01:23:25,772 --> 01:23:27,241
- Take your time packing. - packing.

2157
01:23:27,242 --> 01:23:28,741
I couldn't pack properly.

2158
01:23:28,742 --> 01:23:31,011
Gosh, my precious bag. Thank you.

2159
01:23:31,012 --> 01:23:32,012
- Sure. - Hey.

2160
01:23:32,013 --> 01:23:34,281
It fits your outfit perfectly.

2161
01:23:34,282 --> 01:23:36,621
Later, when you come back from the US,

2162
01:23:36,622 --> 01:23:38,152
- let's grab a meal. - Sure.

2163
01:23:38,282 --> 01:23:39,922
But I feel like...

2164
01:23:41,352 --> 01:23:43,622
(Seriously, Hyun Moo...)

2165
01:23:43,992 --> 01:23:45,961
- You didn't say that to me. - You should come too.

2166
01:23:45,962 --> 01:23:47,091
- You should come too. - What?

2167
01:23:47,092 --> 01:23:48,262
When can you not make it?

2168
01:23:50,462 --> 01:23:52,631
Hyun Moo, you'll be punished by the skies for this.

2169
01:23:52,632 --> 01:23:53,702
(Joking)

2170
01:23:53,802 --> 01:23:55,131
- I mean, - I'm hurt.

2171
01:23:55,132 --> 01:23:56,932
I wanted to avoid making plans on those days.

2172
01:23:58,202 --> 01:23:59,441
Have a safe trip.

2173
01:23:59,442 --> 01:24:00,541
(After promising a meal with Hue)

2174
01:24:00,542 --> 01:24:01,771
- Bye. - Bye.

2175
01:24:01,772 --> 01:24:03,382
It's really heartwarming.

2176
01:24:04,282 --> 01:24:06,011
(To the next after-service place)

2177
01:24:06,012 --> 01:24:07,182
It's already night?

2178
01:24:09,082 --> 01:24:11,482
Gosh, it's 6:30pm already.

2179
01:24:12,182 --> 01:24:14,291
- I was so tired. - You're so diligent.

2180
01:24:14,292 --> 01:24:16,622
- It's been almost 12 hours. - That's right.

2181
01:24:16,792 --> 01:24:18,492
The traffic was really bad.

2182
01:24:18,692 --> 01:24:20,292
It's far.

2183
01:24:21,292 --> 01:24:22,891
I'm giving an after-service the whole day.

2184
01:24:22,892 --> 01:24:23,902
(Exhausted)

2185
01:24:24,602 --> 01:24:26,201
(Driving through the heavy traffic during rush hour)

2186
01:24:26,202 --> 01:24:27,401
I'm finally in Seongsu-dong.

2187
01:24:27,402 --> 01:24:29,001
Gosh, it took so long.

2188
01:24:29,002 --> 01:24:30,242
(Seongdong Bridge, Wansimni-ro)

2189
01:24:30,572 --> 01:24:32,541
(He has arrived at the third place for an after-service.)

2190
01:24:32,542 --> 01:24:33,671
Call.

2191
01:24:33,672 --> 01:24:36,006
(He has arrived at the third place for an after-service.)

2192
01:24:37,609 --> 01:24:38,401
- Hello? - Jae Hyeon.

2193
01:24:38,426 --> 01:24:39,496
Hyun Moo.

2194
01:24:39,542 --> 01:24:41,011
It's Moomoo's after-service.

2195
01:24:41,012 --> 01:24:42,681
(The third guest is Jae Hyeon.)

2196
01:24:42,682 --> 01:24:43,782
Open the door for me.

2197
01:24:44,512 --> 01:24:45,512
(Clicking his tongue)

2198
01:24:47,082 --> 01:24:48,382
What was that just now?

2199
01:24:48,452 --> 01:24:49,621
- I did this. - His greeting.

2200
01:24:49,622 --> 01:24:51,298
He must've been watching me through the screen.

2201
01:24:51,322 --> 01:24:52,762
The screen doesn't come on for that.

2202
01:24:54,722 --> 01:24:56,461
- Right. The screen doesn't come on. - He did it all by himself.

2203
01:24:56,462 --> 01:24:57,631
- The screen doesn't come on. - What was I doing?

2204
01:24:57,632 --> 01:24:59,402
The guard must've been shocked.

2205
01:25:00,502 --> 01:25:02,902
(Entering the parking lot without realizing it)

2206
01:25:03,732 --> 01:25:05,372
(Opening)

2207
01:25:06,772 --> 01:25:08,671
(A huge oven fills the entire trunk.)

2208
01:25:08,672 --> 01:25:09,811
- Unloading it must be hard. - My goodness.

2209
01:25:09,812 --> 01:25:11,042
- It's huge. - Goodness.

2210
01:25:11,342 --> 01:25:14,012
(Struggling)

2211
01:25:14,542 --> 01:25:15,612
Hyun Moo.

2212
01:25:16,652 --> 01:25:19,551
(The third guest appears with a bright smile.)

2213
01:25:19,552 --> 01:25:21,921
The third place for Moomoo's after-service is...

2214
01:25:21,922 --> 01:25:24,352
Jae Hyeon's, the one I got the oven for.

2215
01:25:25,622 --> 01:25:28,692
(Hyun Moo's oven was a troublesome item at the bazaar.)

2216
01:25:29,262 --> 01:25:33,161
(He even baked bungeoppang to promote it.)

2217
01:25:33,162 --> 01:25:35,062
(It's so good, right?)

2218
01:25:35,932 --> 01:25:38,872
(But nobody wanted to buy it.)

2219
01:25:39,672 --> 01:25:41,571
(Jae Hyeon was the only one who showed interest.)

2220
01:25:41,572 --> 01:25:43,772
(The original price was around 3,500 to 4,000 dollars.)

2221
01:25:44,012 --> 01:25:45,741
(I'll give it to you at 1,000 dollars.)

2222
01:25:45,742 --> 01:25:48,282
(I'm in!)

2223
01:25:49,142 --> 01:25:53,652
(He gladly bought it for his friends who are preparing to open a cafe.)

2224
01:25:54,022 --> 01:25:56,251
It was the most expensive item at the bazaar.

2225
01:25:56,252 --> 01:25:57,492
- Right. - That's right.

2226
01:25:58,122 --> 01:25:59,151
Let me give you a hand.

2227
01:25:59,152 --> 01:26:00,421
(The oven finally found its rightful owner.)

2228
01:26:00,422 --> 01:26:02,091
It finally found its owner.

2229
01:26:02,092 --> 01:26:03,791
- Be careful. - Let's put it down here.

2230
01:26:03,792 --> 01:26:04,792
(Careful)

2231
01:26:04,793 --> 01:26:06,502
- One, two, three. We got it. - Gosh!

2232
01:26:07,632 --> 01:26:09,901
- Are all these needed? - They're all yours.

2233
01:26:09,902 --> 01:26:11,732
- Really? - Yes, they're all for you.

2234
01:26:12,172 --> 01:26:13,401
These are the stones.

2235
01:26:13,402 --> 01:26:15,302
- You need these. - What are they for?

2236
01:26:15,402 --> 01:26:16,571
When you bake something.

2237
01:26:16,572 --> 01:26:18,741
I think the rack at the bottom is a really good one.

2238
01:26:18,742 --> 01:26:19,941
- He made it. - I made it.

2239
01:26:19,942 --> 01:26:21,041
- Really? - Yes.

2240
01:26:21,042 --> 01:26:23,352
We finally have someone who recognizes that.

2241
01:26:23,482 --> 01:26:25,081
- After it's sold. - I know.

2242
01:26:25,082 --> 01:26:26,881
So people know its value.

2243
01:26:26,882 --> 01:26:27,882
(Feeling proud)

2244
01:26:28,022 --> 01:26:30,142
- Shall we just move like this? - Yes, let's just go.

2245
01:26:30,852 --> 01:26:32,091
It has wheels.

2246
01:26:32,092 --> 01:26:33,122
Of course.

2247
01:26:34,322 --> 01:26:37,092
(Smoothly moving to the elevator thanks to the wheels)

2248
01:26:37,662 --> 01:26:38,662
Hold on.

2249
01:26:38,662 --> 01:26:39,662
(Pressing)

2250
01:26:40,332 --> 01:26:41,802
I'll leave the doors open.

2251
01:26:43,072 --> 01:26:44,102
No!

2252
01:26:44,502 --> 01:26:45,732
- No way! - What is it?

2253
01:26:46,342 --> 01:26:48,542
(What's waiting for the two behind the doors...)

2254
01:26:48,672 --> 01:26:50,541
(are ten stairs.)

2255
01:26:50,542 --> 01:26:52,371
- It doesn't lead to the elevator. - No, it doesn't.

2256
01:26:52,372 --> 01:26:53,932
- We needed to climb that. - Of course.

2257
01:26:54,442 --> 01:26:55,782
No, it's okay.

2258
01:26:55,982 --> 01:26:57,812
- Are you serious? - I'm serious.

2259
01:26:59,482 --> 01:27:02,522
I thought of taking it back home...

2260
01:27:02,952 --> 01:27:04,951
and hiring someone.

2261
01:27:04,952 --> 01:27:07,392
It's unbearably heavy.

2262
01:27:08,592 --> 01:27:14,202
(He struggled to move it even at his place.)

2263
01:27:14,562 --> 01:27:16,401
- Are you serious? - I'm serious.

2264
01:27:16,402 --> 01:27:17,971
(You want me to climb the stairs?)

2265
01:27:17,972 --> 01:27:19,542
(Next story)

2266
01:27:19,972 --> 01:27:22,602
(In front of Seoul Station at 5am in the morning)

2267
01:27:23,072 --> 01:27:25,111
(CODE KUNST is eagerly waiting for someone.)

2268
01:27:25,112 --> 01:27:26,182
There he is.

2269
01:27:26,882 --> 01:27:28,182
(Hey.)

2270
01:27:28,812 --> 01:27:30,352
(Actor Lee Dong Hwi)

2271
01:27:31,012 --> 01:27:32,052
Hey.

2272
01:27:32,652 --> 01:27:34,382
(Seoul Station TPO of a fashionista?)

2273
01:27:35,222 --> 01:27:37,192
(The place they headed to from the crack of dawn)

2274
01:27:37,422 --> 01:27:39,322
(Busan Station)

2275
01:27:39,522 --> 01:27:41,292
(Filled with block toys that he likes)

2276
01:27:41,662 --> 01:27:44,762
(Visiting a special vintage shop)

2277
01:27:45,162 --> 01:27:46,602
(It opens at 2pm.)

2278
01:27:47,032 --> 01:27:48,832
(At 2pm?)

2279
01:27:48,932 --> 01:27:50,101
If it opens at 2pm...

2280
01:27:50,102 --> 01:27:51,872
(They miscalculated the time big time.)

2281
01:27:52,272 --> 01:27:54,102
(They go shop at vintage shops for now.)

2282
01:27:54,202 --> 01:27:55,741
(They begin searching for treasure.)

2283
01:27:55,742 --> 01:27:56,812
(This is mine.)

2284
01:27:57,572 --> 01:27:59,142
(But I...)

2285
01:27:59,342 --> 01:28:00,411
(My clothes...)

2286
01:28:00,412 --> 01:28:03,352
(are the most vintage here.)

2287
01:28:04,382 --> 01:28:06,082
(Moved by Dong Hwi's taste)

2288
01:28:06,752 --> 01:28:09,792
(They found a destination that wasn't part of their plan.)

2289
01:28:11,422 --> 01:28:12,691
(It's CODE KUNST.)

2290
01:28:12,692 --> 01:28:14,561
(Cat population gap, filled, empty)

2291
01:28:14,562 --> 01:28:15,891
Sung Woo, you're popular.

2292
01:28:15,892 --> 01:28:16,961
(You're popular.)

2293
01:28:16,962 --> 01:28:18,332
(Laughing)

2294
01:28:18,862 --> 01:28:20,262
(Still, they're so cute.)

2295
01:28:20,832 --> 01:28:22,432
(Laughing)

2296
01:28:23,372 --> 01:28:25,432
(Is it okay to be this happy?)

2297
01:28:25,972 --> 01:28:27,901
(The luck given...)

2298
01:28:27,902 --> 01:28:29,182
(to those who didn't plan ahead)

2299
01:28:29,302 --> 01:28:31,111
(There's a block toy shop around here?)

2300
01:28:31,112 --> 01:28:32,112
(Doubtful)

2301
01:28:32,372 --> 01:28:34,542
(Dong Hwi, trust me.)

2302
01:28:35,112 --> 01:28:37,512
(The place that's crazy obsessed with blocks)

2303
01:28:37,712 --> 01:28:38,951
(Incredible history)

2304
01:28:38,952 --> 01:28:39,952
(Incredible scale)

2305
01:28:40,482 --> 01:28:42,521
(A series of precious block toys)

2306
01:28:42,522 --> 01:28:43,551
(It's a shark!)

2307
01:28:43,552 --> 01:28:44,552
(It's a crocodile!)

2308
01:28:44,553 --> 01:28:45,591
(It's a glow-in-the-dark ghost.)

2309
01:28:45,592 --> 01:28:48,662
(Is he spending 10,000 dollars today?)

2310
01:28:48,762 --> 01:28:49,802
(Dong Hwi, it's a monkey!)

2311
01:28:49,862 --> 01:28:50,862
(It's a monkey!)

2312
01:28:50,992 --> 01:28:51,992
(They have a banana too.)

2313
01:28:52,832 --> 01:28:54,461
(I heard you.)

2314
01:28:54,462 --> 01:28:55,502
Dong Hwi.

2315
01:28:55,962 --> 01:28:58,302
(A Build-It-Yourself Day)

2316
01:28:59,302 --> 01:29:00,302
(No!)

2317
01:29:00,902 --> 01:29:03,041
(They're left with...)

2318
01:29:03,042 --> 01:29:04,312
(the oven and stairs.)

2319
01:29:05,412 --> 01:29:07,058
(President Moo's after-service continues.)

2320
